{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"REBAR-DEBUG PHASE 2 — repair and proof complete\n\nRoot cause: accepted `/rerun` and `recheck-review` requests existed only as `_rebar_force` events in the process-local queue. After process loss, Gerrit still carried the old nonzero vote and SQLite still carried the matching `voted` row, so reconciliation skipped the revision before it could recreate the review.\n\nRepair: both acceptance paths now reset the exact current revision to fixed neutral `LLM-Review: 0`, verify all accounts retain no nonzero vote, best-effort reset the retry budget, then enqueue/return the forced live event. The reset-emitted Gerrit `comment-added` event is the durable marker. Reconciliation queries Gerrit before local dedup; a definitive no-vote read clears only the exact stale row, while a Gerrit read error preserves dedup and holds the cursor back. Contributor text cannot select a label value or mint PASS/BLOCK; replies remain label-free. Public policy, ADR, deployment, and operator-runbook documentation now state this contract.\n\nHeld-out proof: `test_accepted_rerun_survives_restart_via_gerrit_reconcile` begins with an old nonzero Gerrit vote, matching stale SQLite dedup, an unrelated dedup row, an exhausted retry budget, and a cursor past the original patchset event. `/rerun` returns 202 and queues once; the old queue is discarded; a replacement queue is empty. One reconcile pass consumes the reset-emitted event and returns `{scanned: 1, reviewed: 1}`, casts exactly one new vote for the exact revision, and preserves the unrelated row.\n\nMutation proof: temporarily restoring the defective local-dedup-first branch made that held-out test fail with `{reviewed: 0}`; restoring Gerrit-first ordering returned it to GREEN.\n\nVerification on current `origin/main`: plan review PASS/certified; focused review-bot/security suite 157 passed; newly-landed base tests 13 passed; `make lint` passed; `make typecheck` passed (491 files); `git diff --check` passed. Clean full CI-extra suite before the final two non-overlapping origin/main commits: 11,732 passed, 19 skipped, 255 deselected in 44m33s with `REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1`. The first full run exposed a missing local `ui` extra (15 audit-page failures due solely to absent jinja2); installing the documented `dev + reviewbot + ui + metrics` extras made that cluster 15/15 green and the subsequent clean full run green.\n\nManual five-axis review found no blocking correctness, security, performance, maintainability, or test issue. One failure-atomicity correction was applied during review: once Gerrit neutral state is durable, a local `reset_attempts` failure is warned but does not falsely reject an already-accepted request."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786377717838999001,"uuid":"2572cb42-6fdd-4bc6-a686-7d063ddf1315"}